---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { doctor, site } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Page
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Terms for using this website and for booking consultations."
  slug="terms"
  updated="2026-10-17"
  intro="The terms on which this website is provided, and the basis on which consultations are booked."
>
  <div class="note note-warn">
    <h3>Before publishing</h3>
    <p>
      This is a working draft prepared alongside the website. It should be reviewed by a lawyer
      before the site goes live, particularly the sections on cancellation and liability.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Using this website</h2>
  <p>
    This website is published by {doctor.name}, {doctor.qualifications}, {doctor.registration}. By
    using it you accept these terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    The content is general medical information, not personal medical advice. Please read the
    <a href="/disclaimer/">medical disclaimer</a>, which forms part of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Content and copyright</h2>
  <p>
    The text on this site is written for this practice and is its copyright. You are welcome to
    read it, print it and share links to it — the diet charts in particular are intended to be
    shared. Republishing substantial portions elsewhere, or presenting it as your own, is not
    permitted.
  </p>

  <h2>Booking a consultation</h2>
  <p>
    Booking a slot, in person or online, is a request for an appointment. An appointment is
    confirmed when you receive confirmation from the clinic.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are asked to provide accurate information about your condition, your medical history and
    any medicines you are taking. A diagnosis made on incomplete or inaccurate information may be
    wrong, and that is a real clinical risk rather than a formality.
  </p>

  <h2>Online consultations</h2>
  <p>
    Online consultations are conducted under India's Telemedicine Practice Guidelines. Your
    identity is verified and your consent is recorded before the consultation begins.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not every condition can be assessed over video. If yours cannot, you will be told at the
    start of the consultation and advised to be seen in person — either at one of the clinics or
    by a doctor near you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Only medicines that the telemedicine rules permit will be prescribed remotely. Some
    medicines require an in-person examination first, and that restriction is not negotiable.
  </p>

  <h2>Fees, cancellation and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Consultation fees are shown before payment is taken. A consultation fee covers the
    consultation itself — the assessment, the explanation and the plan — and not a guaranteed
    outcome.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a consultation cannot be completed usefully online and you are advised to be seen in
    person instead, the consultation fee is not taken.
  </p>
  <p>
    [To be completed before publication: cancellation window, rescheduling policy, and refund
    terms.]
  </p>

  <h2>What this service is not</h2>
  <p>
    This is not an emergency service. If you have a rapidly spreading rash, blistering, a severe
    allergic reaction, or any skin problem with fever or feeling unwell, seek care immediately in
    person rather than booking an online consultation.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits of liability</h2>
  <p>
    We take care that the information published here is accurate at the time of review, but we
    do not warrant that it is complete or current, and we are not liable for decisions taken on
    the basis of it without a consultation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability for professional negligence, which is governed by
    Indian medical law and the applicable regulations.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at Delhi have jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
</Page>
